</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'BottomSheetOptions',
};
</script>

<style scoped>
.option-text {
  font-size: 18;
  padding: 16;
  text-align: center;
  border-color: #eee;
  border-width: 0 0 1 0;
}
</style>
```

4. Use the created 'BottomSheetOptions.vue' component in your main component:

```html
<template>
  <Page class="page">
    <ActionBar title="App" class="action-bar" />
    <StackLayout>
      <Button text="Open bottom sheet" @tap="openBottomSheet()" />
    </StackLayout>
  </Page>
</template>

<script>
import BottomSheetOptions from '~/components/BottomSheetOptions';

export default {
  components: {
    BottomSheetOptions,
  },
  methods: {
    openBottomSheet() {
      this.$showBottomSheet(BottomSheetOptions, {
        closeCallback: (selectedOption) => {
          if (selectedOption) {
            console.log('Selected Option:', selectedOption);
          }
        },
        dismissOnBackgroundTap: true,
        dismissOnDraggingDownSheet: true,
      });
    },
  },
};
</script>
```

This code creates a bottom sheet with 3 options. When an option is tapped, it sends a 'selectedOption' event with the option index and logs the option number in the console. Modify the code according to your preferences to implement the desired functionality.

